1
00:00:02,830 --> 00:00:05,710
- I tell you that girl totally winked at me!         - She did not wink at you.

2
00:00:05,880 --> 00:00:08,880
You always think somebody's winking at you.

3
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:31,800
# So no one told you life was gonna be this way #

4
00:00:32,370 --> 00:00:36,540
# Your job's a joke, you're broke, your love life's D.O.A. #

5
00:00:37,450 --> 00:00:41,260
# It's like you're always stuck in second gear #

6
00:00:41,720 --> 00:00:43,820
# When it hasn't been your day, #

7
00:00:43,820 --> 00:00:46,820
# your week, your month, or even your year #

8
00:00:46,820 --> 00:00:50,780
# but I'll be there for you #

9
00:00:50,780 --> 00:00:52,610
# When the rain starts to pour #

10
00:00:52,610 --> 00:00:55,730
# I'll be there for you #

11
00:00:55,730 --> 00:00:57,570
# Like I've been there before #

12
00:00:57,570 --> 00:01:00,580
# I'll be there for you #

13
00:01:00,580 --> 00:01:04,240
# 'Cause you're there for me too #

14
00:01:11,940 --> 00:01:14,440
I say "Tupelo Honey" by Van Morrison.

15
00:01:14,610 --> 00:01:15,990
No way!

16
00:01:16,150 --> 00:01:18,990
The most romantic song ever was "The Way We Were."

17
00:01:19,160 --> 00:01:24,330
Ah, I think the one that Elton John wrote for, um, that guy on Who's the Boss?

18
00:01:26,330 --> 00:01:28,290
What song was that?

19
00:01:28,460 --> 00:01:31,670
Hold me close, young Tony Danza

20
00:01:36,510 --> 00:01:37,840
- Hi, Monica.     - Hi, Mon.

21
00:01:38,010 --> 00:01:39,680
Hey, Mon.

22
00:01:41,550 --> 00:01:42,970
Oh, my God!

23
00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:44,970
- Has she slept at all?     - Nope.

24
00:01:45,140 --> 00:01:47,060
It's been three nights in a row.

25
00:01:47,230 --> 00:01:49,060
She finally stopped crying yesterday.

26
00:01:49,230 --> 00:01:52,360
But then she found one of Richard's cigar butts on the terrace...

27
00:01:52,520 --> 00:01:56,940
Oh. Okay, that explains it. I got a call at 2 in the morning...

28
00:01:57,110 --> 00:01:59,360
...and all I could hear was this squeaky sound.

29
00:01:59,570 --> 00:02:02,200
So I thought, "Oh, it's a mouse or a possum."

30
00:02:03,870 --> 00:02:07,200
Then I realized, like, okay...

31
00:02:07,370 --> 00:02:11,420
...where would a mouse or a possum get the money to make the phone call?

32
00:02:14,210 --> 00:02:16,630
- Morning.     - Morning. Hey.

33
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:18,630
You made pancakes?

34
00:02:20,050 --> 00:02:22,300
Yeah, like there's any way I could ever do that.

35
00:02:22,930 --> 00:02:26,010
Monica and Rachel had syrup

36
00:02:26,180 --> 00:02:29,430
Uh, uh Now I can get my man to cheer up.

37
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:33,440
Good morning, Joey.

38
00:02:33,610 --> 00:02:34,900
Good morning.

39
00:02:35,940 --> 00:02:37,030
Here's a thought.

40
00:02:37,190 --> 00:02:40,070
Why don't you stay home from work and just hang out with me?

41
00:02:40,240 --> 00:02:41,320
Oh, I wish.

42
00:02:41,490 --> 00:02:44,700
You have that report to finish, and I've got to see my lawyer.

43
00:02:44,870 --> 00:02:48,040
I can't believe I date a girl who's getting divorced.

44
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:50,660
I'm such a grownup.

45
00:02:50,830 --> 00:02:52,540
I gotta go, I gotta go.

46
00:02:52,710 --> 00:02:54,080
Not without a kiss.

47
00:02:54,250 --> 00:02:56,380
Maybe I won't kiss you so you'll stay.

48
00:02:56,550 --> 00:02:58,760
Kiss her. Kiss her!

49
00:03:00,630 --> 00:03:03,220
I'll see you later, sweetie. Bye, Joey.

50
00:03:03,390 --> 00:03:05,430
Bye-bye, Janice.

51
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:09,140
So when are you dumping her?

52
00:03:09,310 --> 00:03:10,390
Nope.

53
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:11,640
Not this time.

54
00:03:11,810 --> 00:03:14,310
Heh. Come on, quit yanking me.

55
00:03:17,650 --> 00:03:19,440
I'm not yanking you.

56
00:03:20,900 --> 00:03:23,030
- This is Janice.     - Yeah, I know.

57
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:24,780
She makes me happy.

58
00:03:26,200 --> 00:03:28,080
Okay. All right.

59
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:31,750
You look me in the eye and tell me, without blinking...

60
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:34,750
...that you're not breaking up with her. No blinking.

61
00:03:37,670 --> 00:03:39,380
I'm not breaking up with her!

62
00:03:46,760 --> 00:03:47,850
What's that?

63
00:03:48,010 --> 00:03:50,520
God, look what I found in the drain!

64
00:03:50,680 --> 00:03:52,140
What?

65
00:03:53,060 --> 00:03:55,520
It's some of Richard's hair!

66
00:03:55,690 --> 00:03:57,230
What do I do with this?

67
00:03:57,400 --> 00:04:00,400
Getting it away from me would be job one.

68
00:04:01,530 --> 00:04:04,660
It's weird, but I don't want to throw this away.

69
00:04:04,820 --> 00:04:06,870
This is all I have left of him.

70
00:04:07,030 --> 00:04:08,620
Gross...

71
00:04:09,370 --> 00:04:10,620
...drain hair.

72
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:22,260
Cool! Oh, it looks like a tiny little person drowning in your cereal.

73
00:04:24,760 --> 00:04:27,800
- God, what is wrong with me?     - You need to get some sleep.

74
00:04:27,970 --> 00:04:29,300
I need to get some Richard.

75
00:04:32,850 --> 00:04:35,060
You broke up with him for a reason.

76
00:04:35,230 --> 00:04:39,230
I know. I know. I'm just so tired of missing him.

77
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:42,530
Tired of wondering why he hasn't called. Why hasn't he called?

78
00:04:42,690 --> 00:04:44,820
Maybe because you told him not to?

79
00:04:45,660 --> 00:04:47,910
What are you, the Memory Woman?

80
00:04:49,700 --> 00:04:51,910
They're not breaking up! Chandler and Janice?

81
00:04:52,080 --> 00:04:54,580
They're not breaking up! He didn't blink!

82
00:04:56,040 --> 00:04:58,500
Well, you koow I'm not surprised. Have you seen them together?

83
00:04:58,670 --> 00:04:59,960
They're really cute.

84
00:05:00,130 --> 00:05:03,090
"Cute"? This is Janice!

85
00:05:03,340 --> 00:05:04,590
You remember Janice?

86
00:05:04,760 --> 00:05:07,260
Yes, I remember. She's annoying. But you know what?

87
00:05:07,430 --> 00:05:10,180
She's his girlfriend now. I mean, what can we do?

88
00:05:10,350 --> 00:05:14,020
There you go! That's the spirit I'm looking for! "What can we do?"

89
00:05:16,020 --> 00:05:18,560
All right, who's first, huh? Ross?

90
00:05:18,730 --> 00:05:21,400
Chandler's our friend, and Janice makes him happy.

91
00:05:21,570 --> 00:05:24,360
So I say we be adult about it and accept her.

92
00:05:24,530 --> 00:05:26,360
We'll call that Plan B.

93
00:05:48,760 --> 00:05:49,930
Honey...

94
00:05:50,090 --> 00:05:52,430
...I was wondering...

95
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:56,430
...do you still have that, um, Navy uniform?

96
00:05:57,850 --> 00:06:00,600
No, I had to return it to the costume place.

97
00:06:02,070 --> 00:06:04,190
I think I have an old band uniform from high school.

98
00:06:05,110 --> 00:06:07,320
You remember not having sex in high school, right?

99
00:06:07,490 --> 00:06:09,360
Yeah.

100
00:06:13,200 --> 00:06:14,620
Well, honey, what about you?

101
00:06:14,790 --> 00:06:15,870
- What?     - I mean...

102
00:06:17,290 --> 00:06:22,290
Do you have any fun, you know, fantasy-type things?

103
00:06:23,290 --> 00:06:24,880
No.

104
00:06:26,300 --> 00:06:28,170
Come on. You gotta have one.

105
00:06:29,130 --> 00:06:30,180
Nope.

106
00:06:31,220 --> 00:06:32,840
- Ross, you know what?     - What?

107
00:06:33,010 --> 00:06:36,720
If you tell me, I might do it.

108
00:06:44,400 --> 00:06:46,150
Okay.

109
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:52,160
Did you ever see, um, Return of the Jedi?

110
00:06:58,160 --> 00:06:59,870
Yeah.

111
00:07:01,170 --> 00:07:03,830
Do you remember the scene...

112
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:07,670
...with, um, Jabba the Hutt?

113
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:13,510
Jabba had as his prisoner...

114
00:07:13,680 --> 00:07:14,890
...Princess Leia.

115
00:07:19,180 --> 00:07:20,850
Princess Leia was wearing...

116
00:07:21,020 --> 00:07:25,690
...this, um, gold bikini thing.

117
00:07:27,980 --> 00:07:30,030
It was pretty cool.

118
00:07:32,700 --> 00:07:36,700
Yeah, Princess Leia and the gold bikini? Oh, every guy our age loved that.

119
00:07:38,700 --> 00:07:40,330
Really?

120
00:07:40,710 --> 00:07:44,420
It's huge! That's the moment when she stopped being a princess...

121
00:07:44,580 --> 00:07:47,420
...and she became, like, you know, a woman.

122
00:07:49,210 --> 00:07:52,220
Did you ever do the Leia thing?

123
00:07:52,380 --> 00:07:53,970
Oh, yeah. Mm-hm.

124
00:07:57,560 --> 00:08:00,270
Really? That great, huh?

125
00:08:00,430 --> 00:08:03,770
No, it's just that I got this new pager, and I have it on "vibrate."

126
00:08:08,900 --> 00:08:10,480
See you.

127
00:08:10,650 --> 00:08:11,740
Hey.

128
00:08:11,900 --> 00:08:12,990
Hi, you guys!

129
00:08:13,150 --> 00:08:15,740
Look who I found standing outside the Szechuan Dragon...

130
00:08:15,910 --> 00:08:18,620
...staring at a parking meter.

131
00:08:18,780 --> 00:08:23,080
- Ahem. Mon. Hi.     - Hi.

132
00:08:23,250 --> 00:08:26,460
- Why aren't you at work?     - Oh, they sent me home.

133
00:08:26,630 --> 00:08:28,130
Why?

134
00:08:28,290 --> 00:08:31,170
Because I don't work at the Szechuan Dragon.

135
00:08:31,380 --> 00:08:33,510
You really need to get some sleep.

136
00:08:33,670 --> 00:08:34,840
I know I do.

137
00:08:35,010 --> 00:08:36,470
- Hi.     - Hi.

138
00:08:36,640 --> 00:08:38,510
Guess what? They published my paper.

139
00:08:38,680 --> 00:08:41,850
Oh! Really? Let me see, let me see.

140
00:08:42,020 --> 00:08:43,230
Rach, look!

141
00:08:43,430 --> 00:08:44,560
No.

142
00:08:44,730 --> 00:08:46,310
Hi. Ha, ha.

143
00:08:49,440 --> 00:08:52,030
Where is my strong Ross Skywalker to come rescue me?

144
00:08:58,450 --> 00:08:59,570
There he is!

145
00:09:04,330 --> 00:09:05,580
- Hey.     - Wheel!

146
00:09:05,750 --> 00:09:08,080
Fortune!

147
00:09:09,210 --> 00:09:10,590
This guy's so stupid.

148
00:09:10,750 --> 00:09:12,250
It's Count Rushmore!

149
00:09:16,470 --> 00:09:18,470
You should really go on this show.

150
00:09:20,220 --> 00:09:24,020
All right, lisen, I got three tickets to the Rangers tonight. What do you say?

151
00:09:24,180 --> 00:09:26,230
I say I am there!

152
00:09:26,390 --> 00:09:28,100
Cool! Oh.

153
00:09:28,270 --> 00:09:29,350
Is Ross going too?

154
00:09:29,520 --> 00:09:30,900
No. Janice.

155
00:09:31,070 --> 00:09:33,110
Janice?

156
00:09:33,860 --> 00:09:37,240
Because I just feel bad for Ross, you know?

157
00:09:37,410 --> 00:09:42,160
We always go together. We're like The Three Hockey-teers, you know?

158
00:09:42,660 --> 00:09:47,210
You koow, I may be way out on a limb here, but do you have a problem with Janice?

159
00:09:47,370 --> 00:09:49,000
No!

160
00:09:49,630 --> 00:09:50,880
Yes...

161
00:09:51,540 --> 00:09:54,170
Oh, God, how do I say this? Uh...

162
00:09:57,550 --> 00:10:00,140
You know that girl from the restaurant with the hair?

163
00:10:00,300 --> 00:10:03,350
Ooh! That girl that I hate? Ugh! She drives me crazy. Ew.

164
00:10:05,520 --> 00:10:09,770
Look, I don't hate Janice. She's just a lot to take, you know?

165
00:10:12,360 --> 00:10:14,730
Well, there you go.

166
00:10:14,940 --> 00:10:16,690
Come on, don't look at me like that.

167
00:10:16,860 --> 00:10:19,320
She drove you nuts before too, remember?

168
00:10:19,530 --> 00:10:22,620
I'm crazy about her now. l think this could be the real thing.

169
00:10:22,780 --> 00:10:24,870
Capital R, capital T!

170
00:10:27,040 --> 00:10:29,710
Don't worry, those are the right letters.

171
00:10:30,460 --> 00:10:33,630
Look, what do you want me to say?

172
00:10:34,420 --> 00:10:36,210
I want you to say that you like her!

173
00:10:36,380 --> 00:10:39,340
I can't. It's like this chemical thing, you know?

174
00:10:39,510 --> 00:10:42,470
Every time she starts laughing, I just wanna...

175
00:10:45,010 --> 00:10:48,390
...pull my arm off so I have something to throw at her.

176
00:10:50,690 --> 00:10:51,770
Thanks for trying.

177
00:10:53,480 --> 00:10:57,480
Oh, and by the way, there is no Count Rushmore!

178
00:10:57,990 --> 00:11:00,900
Then who's the guy that painted the faces on the mountain?

179
00:11:06,740 --> 00:11:08,410
How could you tell her?

180
00:11:08,580 --> 00:11:11,460
I didn't think it would be that big a deal!

181
00:11:11,620 --> 00:11:13,500
Oh. She didn't think it would be a big deal!

182
00:11:13,670 --> 00:11:15,960
Who are you talking to when you do that?

183
00:11:17,250 --> 00:11:21,590
Look, that was supposed to be a private, personal thing between us.

184
00:11:21,760 --> 00:11:26,010
Okay, Ross, Phoebe is my girlfriend, okay? We tell each other everything.

185
00:11:26,180 --> 00:11:28,010
l mean, come on! Guys do the same thing.

186
00:11:28,180 --> 00:11:31,100
I mean, what about all that locker-room stuff?

187
00:11:31,270 --> 00:11:34,150
That's different, okay? That's like, uh, who dated a stripper?

188
00:11:34,310 --> 00:11:37,820
Or who did it on the back of the Staten Island ferry?

189
00:11:38,690 --> 00:11:39,780
- Both of those Joey?     - Yeah.

190
00:11:41,450 --> 00:11:44,530
But you don't talk about your girlfriend...

191
00:11:44,700 --> 00:11:47,910
...and the intimate stuff you do with her.

192
00:11:48,660 --> 00:11:50,790
- Not even with your best friend?     - No.

193
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:52,040
That is so sad.

194
00:11:53,670 --> 00:11:56,130
You're missing out on so much.

195
00:11:56,420 --> 00:11:59,050
I mean, the bonding and the sharing...

196
00:11:59,300 --> 00:12:02,970
...and knowing they're going through the same thing you are.

197
00:12:03,130 --> 00:12:07,640
Oh. So, what, you tell each other everything?

198
00:12:08,470 --> 00:12:09,560
Pretty much.

199
00:12:13,060 --> 00:12:16,020
Did you talk about the Night of Five Times?

200
00:12:19,230 --> 00:12:22,150
Do you tell people about the Night of Five Times?

201
00:12:22,320 --> 00:12:24,650
Uh, honey, that was with Carol.

202
00:12:24,820 --> 00:12:28,070
I know, but it's still worth mentioning, I think.

203
00:12:29,700 --> 00:12:33,200
Relax every muscle in your body.

204
00:12:35,040 --> 00:12:39,170
Listen to the plinky-plunky music.

205
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:42,840
Okay, now close your eyes...

206
00:12:43,010 --> 00:12:46,010
...and think of a happy place.

207
00:12:46,390 --> 00:12:48,050
Tell me your happy place.

208
00:12:48,220 --> 00:12:50,680
Richard's living room, drinking wine.

209
00:12:50,850 --> 00:12:56,060
No, no, no. Not a Richard thing. Just put down the glass and get out.

210
00:12:56,690 --> 00:12:59,190
I'm sorry, but that's my happy place.

211
00:12:59,360 --> 00:13:04,190
Okay, fine. Use my happy place. Just don't move anything in there.

212
00:13:05,530 --> 00:13:06,610
I'll try not to.

213
00:13:06,780 --> 00:13:10,870
Okay. All right, so, you're in a meadow...

214
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:13,910
...millions of stars in the sky...

215
00:13:14,080 --> 00:13:16,120
You think breaking up was a huge mistake?

216
00:13:16,290 --> 00:13:18,710
There are no questions in the happy place.

217
00:13:19,880 --> 00:13:26,380
Just the warm breeze and the moonlight flowing through the trees.

218
00:13:26,550 --> 00:13:28,890
I'll bet he's over me. I'll bet he's fine.

219
00:13:29,050 --> 00:13:32,760
Betting and wagering of any kind are not permitted in the happy place.

220
00:13:33,140 --> 00:13:34,220
Okay?

221
00:13:34,390 --> 00:13:37,890
There's just, you know, the lovely waterfalls...

222
00:13:38,060 --> 00:13:40,610
...and the trickling fountains...

223
00:13:40,770 --> 00:13:45,740
...and the calming sounds of the babbling brook.

224
00:13:45,900 --> 00:13:47,740
Okay, this isn't working.

225
00:13:47,910 --> 00:13:49,450
I'm still awake, and now I have to pee.

226
00:13:51,660 --> 00:13:53,120
So I hear...

227
00:13:53,290 --> 00:13:54,700
...you hate me!

228
00:13:55,910 --> 00:14:00,420
I, uh, never said hate. I was very careful about that.

229
00:14:00,580 --> 00:14:05,840
A little birdie told me you wanting to rip your arm off and throw it at me.

230
00:14:07,300 --> 00:14:11,550
And you got "hate" from that? You're taking a big leap there, I, uh...

231
00:14:11,720 --> 00:14:13,600
All right, fine, fine, fine!

232
00:14:13,760 --> 00:14:17,600
We have got to do something about our little situation here.

233
00:14:17,770 --> 00:14:19,390
So this is my idea.

234
00:14:19,560 --> 00:14:23,480
You and me spending some quality time together.

235
00:14:24,690 --> 00:14:26,030
But what does that...?

236
00:14:26,190 --> 00:14:27,610
For Chandler!

237
00:14:29,150 --> 00:14:30,570
Okay. I'm in.

238
00:14:30,740 --> 00:14:36,740
Okay! This is what we'll call it: Joey and Janice's Day of Fun!

239
00:14:37,620 --> 00:14:39,000
Does it have to be a day?

240
00:14:39,160 --> 00:14:43,630
Yes, because that's how long it takes to love me.

241
00:14:44,170 --> 00:14:48,300
Yeah, I know. Ha. I sleep in the next room.

242
00:14:52,550 --> 00:14:54,550
I went down to the post office...

243
00:14:54,720 --> 00:14:57,640
...and it turns out it was those videos that I ordered...

244
00:14:57,810 --> 00:15:00,810
...for Richard about the Civil War.

245
00:15:00,980 --> 00:15:03,100
He loved the Civil War.

246
00:15:04,730 --> 00:15:07,730
Do you want us to take you home?

247
00:15:11,360 --> 00:15:13,990
Or maybe to a galaxy far, far away.

248
00:15:22,330 --> 00:15:25,170
Women tell each other everything. Did you know that?

249
00:15:25,340 --> 00:15:27,500
Ha, ha. Yeah.

250
00:15:27,880 --> 00:15:30,510
No, Chandler, everything.

251
00:15:31,510 --> 00:15:34,260
Like stuff you like. Stuff she likes.

252
00:15:34,430 --> 00:15:37,850
Technique. Stamina. Girth.

253
00:15:39,180 --> 00:15:40,730
Girth?

254
00:15:41,560 --> 00:15:43,190
Why? Why? Why?

255
00:15:43,350 --> 00:15:45,400
Why would they do this?

256
00:15:46,480 --> 00:15:49,900
Rachel says sharing's great and supposedly...

257
00:15:50,070 --> 00:15:52,570
...we ought to be doing it.

